# Location UX

- Photos are exempt from location capture: no location controls, geolocation
  requests, auto-tagging or saved-location display in the photo flow.
- Removing photo location UI does not strip embedded image metadata. That is
  deferred work in `plans/v2-photo-privacy.md`; never claim it is implemented.

- Display human-readable place names, never raw coordinates. Coordinates remain
  internal for positioning and distance calculations. Offline fallback labels
  must not invent names. Save resolved names with records for offline display.
- Current place-name lookup is opt-in and sends the device fix to BigDataCloud.
  Never call its client endpoint for historical or other members' coordinates.

- Never provide manual latitude or longitude inputs, including error fallbacks.
- Capture current location using browser geolocation, with user permission.
- Show locating, accuracy, unavailable, and permission-denied states with retry.
- Do not silently substitute dummy coordinates or reuse a failed refresh's position.
- Current device location is not another member's live location. Remote positions
  require that member's device to share them with consent.
- Destination selection will use place search or map interaction, not coordinates;
  do not substitute current location for a remote destination.
- Waypoints support map click/center selection as an alternative to GPS. Next-stop
  maps show device position and named suggestions. Never present map pins or
  straight-line distance estimates as verified walking routes.
- Map tiles currently require OpenFreeMap network access. Keep attribution visible
  and do not claim offline map downloads until that feature is implemented.
- Browser geolocation requires HTTPS or localhost. One-shot check-ins are not
  continuous tracking; never describe them as background tracking.
